Summary:

Create a module that displays basic system information by using Linux/POSIX system calls and reading a Linux system file.

1. printHostname()
   gethostname()
   Character arrays (char hostname[256])
   Checking return values (0 = success)

2. printUser()
   getuid()
   User IDs (UID)
   struct passwd
   getpwuid()
   Pointer (struct passwd \*pw)
   -> operator

3. printKernel()
   struct utsname
   uname()
   Accessing structure members using .
   Difference between . and ->

4. printOS()
   File handling
   fopen()
   fgets()
   fclose()
   Reading files line by line
   while loop for unknown number of lines
   strncmp() to compare the beginning of strings
   strchr() and strrchr()
   String parsing
   Replacing the last " with '\0'
